get_id\\\":\\\"AST-09eea296fefe7a21b29874ab\\\",\\\"finding\\\":\\\"The plan makes the title's structural form mandatory — element 4953:6611 must have \\\\\\\"exactly one text child strictly equal to 'Zones corporelles', without leading or trailing whitespace or nested elements; substring, trimmed and whitespace-normalised comparisons are insufficient\\\\\\\" — but AST-09eea296fefe7a21b29874ab expresses only the Figma CONTENT rule EQUALS \\\\\\\"Zones corporelles\\\\\\\" (unit TEXT, tolerance 0). The sole independent observable bound to that assertion is the browser's textContent of the title element, which concatenates all descendant text. A delivery such as <h1 data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4953:6611\\\\\\\"><span>Zones </span><span>corporelles</span></h1> yields textContent exactly \\\\\\\"Zones corporelles\\\\\\\" and therefore satisfies both VISUAL_COMPARE proofs while violating the mandated single-text-child / no-nested-element contract. Leading and trailing whitespace are in fact caught by textContent equality; the nesting clause specifically is not. The clause is consequently enforced only by implementer-authored assertions inside tests/ui.test.js, i.e. by the party whose work is under proof, with no independent observation declared anywhere in the plan.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:127 returns `title: title.textContent` as the only title observable; line 121 selects the node by data-figma-id only.\\\",\\\"scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:85 maps the Figma property `characters` to the observer key `title`, so the measured value for FIGPROP-14eff1f237c41d5b6e0ba677 is textContent.\\\",\\\"PROOF-35ce8927084ad2e8cbf7ddb2 and PROOF-ad9c532104742b73d7c0ef8e expected require only 'exact title text Zones corporelles for element 4953:6611 at both' — no structural child constraint.\\\",\\\"planContract plan_items[].implementation_constraints: 'The element bearing data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4953:6611\\\\\\\" must have exactly one text child equal to \\\\\\\"Zones corporelles\\\\\\\", without leading or trailing whitespace or nested elements'.\\\",\\\"uiAtomicityContract criteria CRT-bb76062f4b554d6f150637bf assertions[0] expected = {\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EQUALS\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tolerance\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"unit\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"TEXT\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Zones corporelles\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"viewports\\\\\\\":[402]} with no structural predicate.\\\",\\\"figma observation manifest C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\hadjo\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\kodjo-vnext-review-5UVNL6\\\\\\\\figma\\\\\\\\observation.json:87-89 confirms the only realized title property is `characters`.\\\"],\\\"required_correction\\\":\\\"Either (a) add an assertion under CRT-bb76062f4b554d6f150637bf expressing the structural title contract (element 4953:6611 has exactly one child node and that node is a text node) and extend the expected text of PROOF-35ce8927084ad2e8cbf7ddb2 and PROOF-ad9c532104742b73d7c0ef8e so the independent observer reports the title element's childNodes length and child nodeType alongside textContent; or (b) if single-text-child form is not to be certified in this disposable scope, delete the 'exactly one text child ... without ... nested elements' wording from the plan implementation_constraints and from the TEST/PROOF expected texts, and record the non-certification explicitly in residual_risks. Do not leave a mandated property whose only enforcement is the implementer's own test.\\\",\\\"dependency_target_indices\\\":[418,424,426,430]},{\\\"category\\\":\\\"UI_ASSERTION_GAP\\\",\\\"target_type\\\":\\\"CRITERION\\\",\\\"target_id\\\":\\\"CRT-69873d7cb74294f37aadeb68\\\",\\\"finding\\\":\\\"The plan raises the inline-style markup contract to a hard, non-negotiable constraint — 'The element bearing data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4478:7209\\\\\\\" must declare width:402px, height:874px, box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0 in its own inline style attribute. CSS classes, stylesheets and <style> blocks do not satisfy this markup contract, even with exact rendered geometry.' — yet CRT-69873d7cb74294f37aadeb68 contains only two GEOMETRY assertions (AST-d3683990ecf1c40d80584969 width=402, AST-ff305af04f3327a5ca31dd35 height=874) whose independent observable is getBoundingClientRect. That measurement is numerically identical for a delivery using the CSS default box-sizing:content-box with no border and no padding, so three of the five mandated declarations (box-sizing, border, padding) have no assertion and no independent proof. The clause stating that exact rendered geometry is explicitly insufficient is therefore unverifiable by any declared obligation: the VISUAL_COMPARE proofs measure only geometry, and the FUNCTIONAL_TEST proofs delegate to implementer-authored assertions in tests/ui.test.js.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:123 `const rect=frame.getBoundingClientRect()` and line 127 returns only `width:rect.width,height:rect.height` — the frame's own style attribute is never read.\\\",\\\"PROOF-ad9c532104742b73d7c0ef8e and PROOF-2a56a91ae0a90f4ddd39c2c8 expected require 'unadjusted getBoundingClientRect of frame 4478:7209: width=402 and height=874' with no declaration-level observation.\\\",\\\"uiAtomicityContract CRT-69873d7cb74294f37aadeb68 assertions contain exactly two entries, both property_type GEOMETRY, expected being the raw Figma EQUALS pt rules.\\\",\\\"planContract plan_items[].implementation_constraints asserts the markup contract is not satisfied by stylesheets 'even with exact rendered geometry', which is precisely the condition the declared proofs cannot distinguish.\\\",\\\"scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:108-117 (assertMarkup) is the only code reading the inline style attribute, and it checks width and height only — not box-sizing, border or padding; it is driver-internal and is not a declared plan proof obligation.\\\"],\\\"required_correction\\\":\\\"